{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019ybT3f4cakURRUtTfTwr56","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-app-developers/concepts/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:40:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Cloud Native Buildpacks (CNCF graduated)\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1 Containerization\", \"D3 Application Delivery\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"buildpacks\", \"builder\", \"base-image\", \"lifecycle\", \"detect\", \"build\", \"export\", \"oci-image\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Cloud Native Buildpacks — concepts (buildpacks.io)\n9\t\n10\tA buildpack is software that transforms application source code into runnable artifacts by analyzing the code and determining the best way to build it. A builder is an OCI image containing an ordered combination of buildpacks and a build-time base image, a lifecycle binary, and a reference to a runtime base image. Base images: the build image is the environment in which the buildpacks run; the run image is the base for the final application image; the pairing is the stack. The platform (for example the pack CLI, or a CI system) orchestrates the process by invoking the lifecycle binary together with buildpacks and app source code to produce a runnable OCI image. The lifecycle runs in phases — detect (determine which buildpacks apply), build (compile and assemble the application), export (create the final OCI image with reproducible layers). Cloud Native Buildpacks is a Cloud Native Computing Foundation graduated project.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0c94597-093c-418d-80f7-700be3d3f663","uuid":"687baf66-e61d-47ac-a916-27d1d0c5e74a","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:44:01.354Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\buildpacks-concepts-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-app-developers/concepts/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:40:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Cloud Native Buildpacks (CNCF graduated)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1 Containerization\", \"D3 Application Delivery\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"buildpacks\", \"builder\", \"base-image\", \"lifecycle\", \"detect\", \"build\", \"export\", \"oci-image\"]\n---\n# Cloud Native Buildpacks — concepts (buildpacks.io)\n\nA buildpack is software that transforms application source code into runnable artifacts by analyzing the code and determining the best way to build it. A builder is an OCI image containing an ordered combination of buildpacks and a build-time base image, a lifecycle binary, and a reference to a runtime base image. Base images: the build image is the environment in which the buildpacks run; the run image is the base for the final application image; the pairing is the stack. The platform (for example the pack CLI, or a CI system) orchestrates the process by invoking the lifecycle binary together with buildpacks and app source code to produce a runnable OCI image. The lifecycle runs in phases — detect (determine which buildpacks apply), build (compile and assemble the application), export (create the final OCI image with reproducible layers). Cloud Native Buildpacks is a Cloud Native Computing Foundation graduated project.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
