{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UVxPhEGudKcX2brZEdVyqM","type":"tool_result","content":"372\t## Cross-cutting retrieval themes\n373\t\n374\tNine themes are retrieved by name across the book. **[B3]** established the count and specified the first three; the remaining six are **[B5-reconstructed]** from B2's dependency graph and cross-bearing pairs, and should be reconciled if B3 is re-run.\n375\t\n376\t| # | Theme | Chapter path | Source |\n377\t|---|---|---|---|\n378\t| 1 | **The control loop** — desired state, current state, reconciliation | 3 → 4 → 6 → 11 → 15 → 17 | **[B3]** |\n379\t| 2 | **Namespaced vs cluster-scoped** — *derives* the RBAC four-way matrix instead of memorizing it | 4 → 8 → 12 | **[B3]** |\n380\t| 3 | **\"The object exists but nothing happens without the component\"** — Ingress without a controller, NetworkPolicy on an unsupporting CNI, `kubectl top` without metrics-server, VPA not shipped by default | 10 → 13 → 17 | **[B3]** |\n381\t| 4 | **Declarative desired state vs imperative command** | 4 → 6 → 14 → 15 | [B5-reconstructed] |\n382\t| 5 | **Labels and selectors as the universal join** — ReplicaSet→Pod, Service→Pod, NetworkPolicy→Pod; and the contrast that RBAC uses subjects, not selectors | 4 → 6 → 7 → 9 → 10 → 12 | [B5-reconstructed] |\n383\t| 6 | **Pluggable interfaces** — CRI, CNI, CSI, CRDs as one extensibility story | 2 → 9 → 11 → 6 → 17 | [B5-reconstructed] |\n384\t| 7 | **Identity** — ServiceAccount as the thread from Pod to API to delivery agent | 5 → 12 → 15 | [B5-reconstructed] |\n385\t| 8 | **Requests and limits** — the numbers that reappear everywhere | 5 → 7 → 13 → 17 → 18 | [B5-reconstructed] |\n386\t| 9 | **Additive, allow-only, no deny** — RBAC and NetworkPolicy share one semantic | 10 → 12 | [B5-reconstructed] |\n387\t\n388\tTheme 3 is a *pattern*, not a fact. **[B3]** Name it once in Ch 10 and retrieve it by name afterward; that converts four separate gotchas into one rule.\n389\t\n390\t### Do not retrieve **[B3]**\n391\t\n392\tFour things are excluded from the retrieval schedule entirely:\n393\t\n394\t1. **Ch 1 exam mechanics.** No item anywhere tests them.\n395\t2. **The dated graduated-project roster.** Retrieve the maturity *levels* instead — the roster changes between printing and exam day.\n396\t3. **The 60-question and 75% figures.** Unpublished and commonly-reported; retrieving them would teach them as fact.\n397\t4. **Any `[inferred]` trap framed as exam frequency.** Fourteen of B1's 114 traps are `[inferred]` rather than `[source]`. Those may be described as \"easy to confuse,\" never \"frequently tested\" — Ethical Guardrail #8.\n398\t\n399\t---\n400\t\n401\t## Cross-chapter callback map\n402\t\n403\tRetrieval percentage per chapter, with source range and the mandatory named anchors. Percentages are **[B3]**; the ≥4-back column enforces B3's spacing floor, active from Ch 8 onward.\n404\t\n405\t| Ch | % | Draws from | Mandatory named anchors | ≥4-back item |\n406\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n407\t| 1 | — | — | *excluded from schedule* | — |\n408\t| 2 | — | — | *first content chapter* | — |\n409\t| 3 | 10% | 2 | CRI boundary; image immutability | n/a |\n410\t| 4 | 15% | 2–3 | Control loop; apiserver in `apply` | n/a |\n411\t| 5 | 20% | 2–4 | `imagePullPolicy`; spec/status vs Pod phase | n/a |\n412\t| 6 | 20% | 3–5 | Control loop → named controller; selectors; probes | n/a |\n413\t| 7 | 20% | 4–6 | Node labels; requests as filter input | n/a |\n414\t| 8 | 20% | 3–7 | Namespaces under ResourceQuota; node conditions | **Ch 2 CRI or Ch 3 control loop** |\n415\t| 9 | 20% | 5–8 | Selectors → Service; controller churn | **Ch 5 Pod network namespace** |\n416\t| 10 | 20% | 6–9 | Service-type ladder; what Ingress replaces | **Ch 4 labels/selectors** |\n417\t| 11 | 20% | 6–10 | StatefulSet loop closed; ConfigMap/Secret as volumes | **Ch 5 Pod volumes / Ch 6 StatefulSet** |\n418\t| 12 | 20% | 7–11 | NetworkPolicy cross-beared; ServiceAccount collected | **Ch 4 namespaced/cluster-scoped; Ch 8 admission gate** |\n419\t| 13 | **25%** | all | **Version skew (Ch 8)**; **Pending → scheduling (Ch 7)**; OOMKilled → limits (Ch 5); ImagePullBackOff (Ch 2); `kubectl top` → theme 3 | Ch 2, 5, 7, 8 |\n420\t| 14 | 20% | 9–13 | Ch 6 rollback vs Helm rollback | **Ch 4 `apply`; Ch 6 workload resources** |\n421\t| 15 | **25%** | all | **Control loop (Ch 3) — the Zenith**; rolling-update mechanics (Ch 6); Helm as Argo input (Ch 14); ConfigMap/Secret as factor III (Ch 4) | Ch 3, 4, 6 |\n422\t| 16 | **25%** | all | Ch 13 handoff; Pod phases (Ch 5); Service→EndpointSlice (Ch 9); StatefulSet+PVC (Ch 6, 11) | Ch 5, 6, 9 |\n423\t| 17 | **25%** | all | **CRI/CNI/CSI/CRDs (2, 9, 11, 6) — the Zenith**; **release cadence + version skew (Ch 8)**; **unschedulable → CA (Ch 7)**; metrics-server (Ch 13); VPA → theme 3 | Ch 2, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11 |\n424\t| 18 | **25%** | all | metrics-server vs monitoring (Ch 13); probes ≠ observability (Ch 5); log agents as DaemonSets (Ch 6); mesh telemetry (Ch 17) | Ch 5, 6, 13 |\n425\t| 19 | ~100% | all | All nine themes by name; every surviving confusion pair | all |\n426\t| 20 | weighted | all | Terminal assessment | all |\n427\t\n428\t### Reciprocal cross-bearing pairs to build deliberately\n429\t\n430\tSix pairs must be built as pairs — each half written knowing the other exists, per B2:\n431\t\n432\t| Pair | Relationship |\n433\t|---|---|\n434\t| Ch 6 ↔ Ch 11 | StatefulSet introduced / PV pairing completed — the book's one deliberate forward reference |\n435\t| Ch 10 ↔ Ch 12 | NetworkPolicy taught once in Ch 10; Ch 12 cross-bears in as the network half of security |\n436\t| Ch 13 ↔ Ch 16 | Troubleshooting handoff — platform scope hands off, application scope hands back |\n437\t| Ch 4 → Ch 15 | ConfigMap/Secret as twelve-factor factor III |\n438\t| Ch 3 → Ch 6 → Ch 15 | The control-loop spine, three beats |\n439\t| Ch 13 → Ch 17 and Ch 13 → Ch 18 | metrics-server as autoscaler input; metrics pipeline vs monitoring |\n440\t\n441\t### Decay fixes — do not drop\n442\t\n443\tThree chapters teach dense material that is otherwise never revisited. **[B3]** identified these and placed the anchors; drafting must honor them.\n444\t\n445\t| At risk | Why | Where it is retrieved |\n446\t|---|---|---|\n447\t| **Ch 8 version skew** | Densest pure-recall block in the book, taught at the 40% mark | Ch 13 (as a troubleshooting cause) **and** Ch 17 (release cadence + three-supported-minors, which explain each other) |\n448\t| **Ch 7 scheduling** | Thin downstream presence | Ch 13 (Pending as a scheduling-failure signature) **and** Ch 17 (Cluster Autoscaler reacting to unschedulable Pods) |\n449\t| **Ch 14 Helm** | Thin downstream presence | Ch 15 (charts as Argo's manifest source) **and** Ch 17 (CRDs shipped as chart content) |\n450\t\n451\t### Soundings do the spacing work for free **[B3]**\n452\t\n453\tSoundings are **excluded from the retrieval budget** but perform retrieval anyway. Skill Part 11 requires Soundings questions be answerable from prerequisites — which in this book *means earlier chapters*. Counting them against the 20–25% target would distort their calibration purpose. **The drafting instruction is therefore: source each chapter's Soundings from B2's Prerequisites column**, which makes every Soundings block a spaced retrieval event at no cost to the schedule.\n454\t\n455\t---\n456\t\n457\t## Open items carried into drafting\n458\t\n459\t1. **Re-run B3 or accept the reconstruction.** Six of nine cross-cutting themes here are B5-reconstructed. They are defensible, but they are not B3's list.\n460\t2. **Fetch the LFS250 syllabus (G37) before anything else.** It is the closest artifact to a detailed CNCF objective list. If it changes the weighting, the per-chapter percentages in B2 — and therefore every Practice Qs figure in B4 and every depth band here — should be revised before drafting. The chapter *sequence* is dependency-driven and would not change.\n461\t3. **Seventeen blocking gaps remain open**, routed per chapter in B2 § \"Gap routing.\" Highest-risk single gap is **G2** (Pod failure signatures by name), which gates Ch 13 and Ch 16.\n462\t4. **B4 flagged a skill defect.** Part 8's practice-question formula returns a negative pool (−86) for this book, because fixed baselines alone (326) exceed `300 − mock_size`. It should be restated as a floor-check plus a weight-proportional allocation. KCNA is the first book in the catalog to trip it; any book with ≥13 content chapters and a mock under ~100 questions will trip it too.\n463\t5. **Diagram enforcement is off** for this book (`diagram_enforcement.enabled: false`). The figure anchors above are stubs for the Stage 10 image-spec extraction and the sibling `certcomp-diagrams` pipeline; flip the gate only after that book's diagram retro completes.\n464\t\n465\t---\n466\t\n467\t## Handoff to chapter pipeline\n468\t\n469\tThis arc outline is the authoritative input to `python pipeline/orchestrator.py --run --book kcna --chapter N`. Each chapter's planning stage (stage 1) reads this file and expands its chapter entry into a full outline with section plan.\n470\t\n471\tStage 1 consumes, per chapter: **Covers** (objective mapping), **Prerequisites** (both the chapter refs and the named concepts), **Key concepts introduced** (Fixed Point candidates), **Retrieval targets** (the spacing contract — percentage *and* named anchors, both binding), **Required figures** (anchor stubs, to be expanded into `yaml-figure-spec` blocks at Stage 10), and **Question budget** (Soundings / Bearings / Practice, where Bearings is a minimum to exceed).\n472\t\n473\tStage 1 must **not** derive a word target from the **Target length** field. The depth band is a relative planning signal only; word budgets were retired 2026-04-24 and no downstream stage enforces them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0c94597-093c-418d-80f7-700be3d3f663","uuid":"a89f8c85-aaf7-4e4d-a4f9-4530c1227910","timestamp":"2026-08-